ademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=6.$ So, $x=6$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=6.$ So, $x=6$ has *even* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=6$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity." 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244353 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244354 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244355 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244356 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244357 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1041 "selection" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244357 13194139533654 true] [17592186244352 1110 #uuid "79d0d74d-5e5c-5eb2-a0d5-289806ef2da9" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244353 1034 "$x=6$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244353 1111 #uuid "c9b87d64-2b65-58b6-aebe-7ec8ca563ada" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244354 1034 "$x=6$ is not a root of $p(x)$" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244354 1111 #uuid "555077fb-711f-5f11-929e-2520a27f8729" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244355 1034 "$x=6$ is a simple root" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244355 1111 #uuid "679e573a-c099-5325-b53f-a8b1dc965f86" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244356 1034 "$x=6$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244356 1111 #uuid "097d06b5-3c5e-5df7-9929-14d09fd4ef5e" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244357 1034 "$x=6$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244357 1111 #uuid "b30682d7-1be7-57d5-9349-a11f70085629" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244359 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1089 "q-38680" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/682105815047990048e100ea59c2652e48c0deea8c8caa422bfe3efca7d11c65.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are correct?\n\n- $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n- $x=-1$ is a simple root.\n- $x=2$ is a root of even multiplicity." 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1113 #uuid "dabea786-8408-5b31-8a47-8665b8cf6666" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1138 false 13194139533654 true] [17592186244358 1145 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The root $x=-1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244360 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244361 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244362 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244363 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244364 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1041 "selection" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244361 13194139533654 true] [17592186244359 1110 #uuid "4ac26998-6f00-53e0-a2de-939d74eed232" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244360 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244360 1111 #uuid "20d36a72-f50d-5f0c-b0fe-8dfca7aa7246" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244361 1034 "I only" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244361 1111 #uuid "c421830f-d672-591f-936f-7841571e829e" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244362 1034 "III only" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244362 1111 #uuid "4b1ff5c9-ae03-5578-886d-cf9c77888723" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244363 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244363 1111 #uuid "a84e8d3d-325f-55fb-be6f-c332072f47ed" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244364 1034 "II only" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533654 true] [17592186244364 1111 #uuid "760d168b-bd98-548a-9e1a-836ac1db5d5d" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244365 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244366 13194139533654 true] [17592186244365 1089 "q-38770" 13194139533654 true] [17592186244365 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533654 true] [17592186244365 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/139